{/* ── The about page's marks (2026-10-13) ──
    Phosphor Duotone (MIT, phosphoricons.com), with one borrowed drum. Hiro's
    pick from the icon lab, replacing the 08-04 hand-drawn set — 2px square
    caps to match the contact icons, which read as thin and stiff once the
    toolbox below went to solid brand marks. Duotone is still a line drawing
    but carries a 20% tint of its own colour, which brings the row up to the
    toolbox's weight without turning it into silhouettes.

    These replaced 👋🥁👾🎬🥾 on 08-04 (OS emoji take no --ink-*, can't follow
    the theme, and render differently per platform), and the rule then was
    that each mark redraws ITS OWN emoji rather than a neighbouring idea.
    One exception now, Hiro's call: 👾 became a game controller. Phosphor's
    alien (the nearest thing to an invader) didn't fit, and the controller
    is the plainest read of "video game design" at 20px.

    Phosphor has no drum, so that one is Lucide's (ISC), the nearest in hand
    — but at Phosphor's WEIGHT, not Lucide's: stroke-width 1.5 of 24 is
    Phosphor's 16 of 256, where Lucide's own 2 read visibly heavier than its
    neighbours (Hiro, 10-13). Lucide has no duotone, so the drum's tint is
    ADDED — a shell-shaped fill at Phosphor's own .2 opacity, laid under
    Lucide's strokes (Hiro, 10-13: without it the drum read
    darker and busier than its neighbours). That fill is the only
    hand-drawn path in this block; every other path is verbatim from its
    set, so re-fetch rather than hand-edit. Colour
    is the --mark-* tokens in global.css; the wave stays uncoloured. */}
{
